  "content": {
    "id": "v2-350bda-p6-practice-j23-100008-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Consider the expressions $5a+5a^2$ and $10a^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-350bda-p6-practice-j23-100008-j23-q-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $5a+5a^2$ when $a=2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$30$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5a+5a^2&=5(2)+5(2)^2\\\\&=10+20\\\\&=30\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-350bda-p6-practice-j23-100008-j23-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $10a^2$ when $a=2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$40$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}10a^2&=10(2)^2\\\\&=40\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-350bda-p6-practice-j23-100008-j23-q-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Use your answers to explain why $5a+5a^2$ cannot be written as $10a^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "When $a=2$ the expressions have different values ($30$ and $40$), so they are not equivalent.",
          "worked": "If $5a+5a^2$ were equal to $10a^2$, they would have the same value for every $a$. When $a=2$ they give $30$ and $40$, so $5a$ and $5a^2$ are not like terms and cannot be combined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-350bda-p6-practice-j23-100008-j23-q-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Hayley tests $a=1$ and says the two expressions are equal. Why does this not show that $5a+5a^2$ can be written as $10a^2$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "They happen to agree when $a=1$ (both $10$), but one matching value does not make them equivalent; $a=2$ shows they differ.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5(1)+5(1)^2&=10\\\\10(1)^2&=10\\end{align*}$$\nThe values agree at $a=1$ only by coincidence. Expressions are equivalent only if they agree for every value of $a$, and $a=2$ gives $30\\neq40$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
